Conversion rules between `*T` and `&T`
======================================

Per the reference's "Conversion Rules":

  - `ref -> ptr`: `&r` (unsafe, no refcount change). A `*T`
    derived from a `&T` doesn't extend the ref's lifetime;
    if the ref drops, the pointer dangles.

  - `ptr -> ref`: **always an error.** You can't manufacture
    a refcount from a raw pointer. Enforced at the analyzer.

Status today: **`&r` where r: &T fails on every backend** —
the analyzer/interpreter return a `RefVal` instead of a
`PtrVal`, and subsequent field access through the resulting
"*T" mishandles the value. None of the seven backends
implement the conversion end-to-end.

We don't pin runtime behaviour here until the conversion is
implemented. The file exists to flag the gap and hold a TODO
for the future test:

